          "literatureReview": "Rheumatoid Factor (RF) detects IgM antibodies against IgG Fc portion. Normal: <14 IU/mL. Positive: ≥14 IU/mL. Present in 70-80% of RA patients. Also positive in Sjögren's syndrome, SLE, scleroderma, and infections. Higher titers correlate with disease severity. Used with anti-CCP for RA diagnosis (ACR/EULAR criteria). False positives with age, infections, or other autoimmune diseases. Quantitative measurement preferred over qualitative. Critical for rheumatoid arthritis diagnosis and monitoring."
